 "description": "The map of the UBL example world: routes, towns, fields, forests and the relief, on a grid of 256 x 192 squares of 3.5 km (tools/world_model.py, GRID). tools/world_model.py builds the tile model from it and from the parties. Stations are the pipelines' border metering stations. Towns and localities (villages) give their population (for the villages the decided range) and the width of their built-up area in km (built_km, owner 2026-11-18, O92): the model draws a built-up area of that size around the centre c. Localities give the parties outside the towns a place in their address. The relief gives the height of the ground (control points, cliff coasts, the river's heights along its course). The drawn map is a diagram (O82): it may stretch distances, and Lisavu, about 1,000 km east of Lumeport, is drawn nearer, in its own part of the grid with open sea all round, as an inset.",
